---
import Site from "../layouts/Site.astro";
import Term from "../components/Term.astro";
import TileMapLimits from "../components/TileMapLimits.astro";
import ChartCollect from "../components/ChartCollect.astro";
import "../styles/features.css";
import { steps } from "../lib/steps";
import { states } from "../lib/data";
import { limitStats, feeStats, denver, statesChecked, evidenceChecked, usd } from "../lib/stats";
---
<Site title="Fair Claim">
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Small claims court, explained</p>
    <h1>What small claims court is, what it costs, and what happens after a judgment</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Free, neutral information about small claims court in every US state, with a source and a date next to each
      rule. It covers the costs and the odds of getting paid as plainly as the steps, so you can decide whether it's
      worth it for you.
    </p>
    <form class="state-picker" action="/states/" method="get" data-state-picker>
      <label class="sr-only" for="s">Your state</label>
      <select id="s" name="s">
        <option value="">Choose your state…</option>
        {states.map((s) => <option value={s.slug}>{s.state}</option>)}
      </select>
      <button class="btn" type="submit">See your state's rules</button>
    </form>
    <p class="hint">
      Or browse <a href="/states/">all states</a>. Legal information, not legal advice. Free, no ads, no tracking.
    </p>
  </section>

  <h2>The basics</h2>
  <div class="home-facts">
    <section class="home-fact" aria-labelledby="fact-what">
      <h3 id="fact-what">What it is</h3>
      <p class="figure">{usd(limitStats.min)} to {usd(limitStats.max)}</p>
      <p>
        A simpler part of the court system for smaller money disputes, where people usually speak for themselves. The
        most you can claim depends on the state, from {usd(limitStats.min)} in {limitStats.minStates.join(", ")} to
        {" "}{usd(limitStats.max)} in {limitStats.maxStates.join(" and ")}.
      </p>
      <p class="cite"><a href="/states/">State research, 50 states + DC</a><span>checked {statesChecked}</span></p>
    </section>
    <section class="home-fact" aria-labelledby="fact-cost">
      <h3 id="fact-cost">What it costs</h3>
      <p class="figure">{usd(feeStats.lowest)} to {usd(feeStats.highest)} to file</p>
      <p>
        The <Term slug="filing-fee" /> varies this much across states and claim sizes; in half the states it starts at
        {" "}{usd(feeStats.medianLowest)} or less. Add <Term slug="service-of-process">serving the papers</Term>, time off
        for the hearing, and more fees to collect if you aren't paid. A <Term slug="fee-waiver" /> can help if you can't
        afford them.
      </p>
      <p class="cite"><a href="/about/#chart-fees">Fees by state</a><span>checked {statesChecked}</span></p>
    </section>
    <section class="home-fact" aria-labelledby="fact-paid">
      <h3 id="fact-paid">Winning isn't getting paid</h3>
      <p class="figure">{denver.collectedNothingPct}% collected nothing</p>
      <p>
        That's the share of winners in a study of Denver's small claims court, where only {denver.dollarsPaidPct}% of
        the money awarded was ever paid. A <Term slug="judgment" /> is a right to be paid; the court doesn't collect it
        for you.
      </p>
      <p class="cite"><a href={denver.source.url} rel="noopener">Fordham Urban Law Journal (1994)</a><span>checked {evidenceChecked}</span></p>
    </section>
  </div>

  <h2 id="data">What the data shows</h2>
  <p class="section-intro">
    Numbers from our state-by-state research and the few studies that exist. Each chart names its source and when we
    checked it, and each has a table version.
  </p>
  <TileMapLimits />
  <ChartCollect />
  <p><a class="link-arrow" href="/about/#data">More charts: fees, appeals, recent changes and who uses small claims</a></p>

  <h2>Other ways to settle a dispute</h2>
  <p class="section-intro">Court is one option. These can be tried first, and are often quicker and cheaper.</p>
  <ul class="routes">
    <li>
      <strong>Ask in writing</strong>
      <p>A calm <Term slug="demand-letter" /> with the amount and a deadline settles many disputes, and some courts ask whether you sent one. <a href="/demand-letter/">Write one</a>.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Mediation</strong>
      <p>A neutral person helps you both reach an agreement. In the studies above, mediated agreements were paid more often than judges' decisions.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>A complaint to a regulator</strong>
      <p>For a licensed business, such as a contractor, a complaint to the licensing board or a consumer agency is another route.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Letting it go</strong>
      <p>After the time, the fees and the odds of collecting, some claims aren't worth pursuing. That's a reasonable choice too.</p>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>If you go ahead: the five steps</h2>
  <ol class="strip">
    {steps.map((s) => (
      <li>
        <span class="n">Step {s.n}</span>
        <a class="t" href={`/steps/#${s.slug}`}>{s.title}</a>
        <span class="d">{s.short}</span>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ol>

  <h2>Tools</h2>
  <div class="grid">
    <a class="card card-link" href="/worth-it/">
      <h3>Is it worth it?</h3>
      <p>Put in the amount, your state's fees and a chance of collecting, and see the likely result in dollars.</p>
      <span class="go">Open the calculator</span>
    </a>
    <a class="card card-link" href="/demand-letter/">
      <h3>Demand letter</h3>
      <p>A calm, clear letter asking for payment. It runs in your browser; nothing is stored.</p>
      <span class="go">Write a letter</span>
    </a>
    <a class="card card-link" href="/checklists/">
      <h3>Checklists</h3>
      <p>Printable lists for each step, with your state's limit, fees and deadlines filled in.</p>
      <span class="go">Open the checklists</span>
    </a>
    <a class="card card-link" href="/glossary/">
      <h3>Glossary</h3>
      <p>Plain-English meanings of words like service, default judgment and writ of execution.</p>
      <span class="go">Look up a word</span>
    </a>
    <a class="card card-link" href="/states/ca/counties/">
      <h3>California, county by county</h3>
      <p>Courthouses, self-help centers and free small claims advisor help in all 58 counties.</p>
      <span class="go">California counties</span>
    </a>
  </div>

  <div class="callout info" style="margin-top: var(--space-6)">
    <p>
      <strong>Being sued instead?</strong> A guide for people who've been sued — most often by a debt collector — is
      planned for a later version. Until then, don't ignore the papers: missing your court date usually means losing
      automatically (a <Term slug="default-judgment" />). Your state's court self-help page (linked on every state page)
      explains how to respond.
    </p>
  </div>
</Site>

<script>
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLFormElement>("[data-state-picker]").forEach((f) => {
    f.addEventListener("submit", (e) => {
      e.preventDefault();
      const sel = f.elements.namedItem("s") as HTMLSelectElement;
      if (sel.value) location.href = `/states/${sel.value}/`;
      else sel.focus();
    });
  });
</script>
